      en: "The Maardu Industrial Area is located just east of Tallinn and serves as one of Estonia's premier logistics and manufacturing hubs. Formerly a center for Soviet heavy chemical production, Maardu has evolved since 1991 into a sophisticated node for international trade and cargo transit. Its strategic prominence is largely due to its immediate proximity to Muuga Harbor, the largest and deepest commercial port in Estonia. In addition to extensive warehousing facilities for transit goods, the industrial zone hosts significant enterprises in food processing and metal fabrication. Superb connectivity to the Tallinn-Narva highway and the national rail network ensures efficient transport links toward Northern Europe and Central Asia. Maardu acts as a key engine for economic growth within Harju County, characterized by a diverse, multicultural population whose livelihoods have been historically intertwined with the area's industrial expansion.",
