      en: ["Established in 1992 as the first in the Baltics.", "Home to over 70 innovative companies.", "Works in close cooperation with University of Tartu.", "Headquarters of the ESA Incubation Centre Estonia.", "Features 12,000 m² of laboratory and office space.", "Focused on biotechnology and space industry."],
      es: ["Fundado en el año 2000.", "Más de 100 empresas residentes.", "Emplea a unos 1.500 trabajadores.", "Superficie: 15 hectáreas.", "Alberga la Universidad de Tartu.", "Contiene un laboratorio BSL-2."],
